WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.938
Order decides whether modernization
is a gain or a regression.

2
00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:07.947
Step zero: bring the governor
under vulnerability management,

3
00:00:07.947 --> 00:00:09.951
privileged access and logging.

4
00:00:09.951 --> 00:00:12.272
Then buy the pipe on measured physics,

5
00:00:12.272 --> 00:00:15.267
deploy the governor before
production traffic,

6
00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:18.563
decide the boundary change
before the first cutover,

7
00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:23.206
handle Microsoft 365 through its own
exception, and register the evidence,

8
00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:27.400
confirming CISA telemetry parity
before any legacy circuit ends.

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.313
No memo mandates that order;
it's an engineering dependency.

10
00:00:31.313 --> 00:00:35.762
Phase inversion is what happens when
cloud migration runs ahead of transport.

11
00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:39.851
With no transport metrics, slowness
is attributed to the cloud,

12
00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:44.175
the remedies raise cloud spend, and
the cause never enters the data.

13
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:47.650
The book labels that an inference
built on documented parts,

14
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.013
and names better-evidenced competitors.

15
00:00:50.013 --> 00:00:51.775
So measure in your own estate.

16
00:00:51.775 --> 00:00:56.751
A paired-branch study, two comparable
branches instrumented for 30 days before

17
00:00:56.751 --> 00:01:01.490
and after a change at one, gives an effect
size a budget examiner will accept.
